# SABOTAGE: PP-8/PP-9 (Batch 3, NAV-REACHABILITY) — the Settings + Automation nav items.
# Removes the "Workspace" nav_group (Settings + Automation) from `Samen.UI.Nav.module_nav/1`,
# restoring the exact W3 HIGH-1/HIGH-2 defect: Settings (Profile/API keys/Security/
# Invitations) and Automation (the T118 workflow builder) are total nav islands — real,
# shipped, non-stub features reachable ONLY by hand-typing their URL, with no item anywhere
# in the inherited sidebar every CRM/Billing/Support/Marketing/Notifications/Files/Search
# page renders. The two named PP-8/PP-9 reachability tests FLIP (the items are simply gone
# from the rendered nav); `host_nav_extra/1` and its own tests are UNTOUCHED by this patch —
# the flip isolates exactly the Settings/Automation nav-item guarantee.
# Re-anchored (X1 / ADR-045 §4.1): the Workspace group is now `:if`-gated on the mounted
# `surfaces` set and its items are multi-line; the deletion targets that current shape.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/ui/components_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: module_nav/1 renders a Settings nav item pointing at the settings route (PP-8)
# MUST_FAIL: module_nav/1 renders an Automation nav item pointing at the automation route (PP-9)
